+// Patched copy of the vanilla 26.3 class (stage-2 W7, instant UI transitions; docs/metal/CONTRACT.md 16.W7). Differences
+// from vanilla, all behind UiTransitions.instant (-Dmc.ui.instantTransitions, default on; off = vanilla, read once per overlay):
+//  - tick(): once the completion callback has run (same moment as vanilla) and the screen below was re-initialized (same
+//    call), the overlay removes itself (only if it is still the current overlay) instead of fading out for 2.0 s; in a world
+//    (the callback discarded all compiled terrain) it first stays opaque until UiTransitions.terrainShown has held for
+//    IN_WORLD_STABLE_TICKS ticks, at most IN_WORLD_HOLD_CAP_MS (vanilla's fade-out) after the callback;
+//  - isReadyToFadeOut(): no 1.0 s minimum hold on later reloads (fadeIn), EXCEPT while a server / world resource-pack reload
+//    is pending (DownloadedPackSource.serverPackReloadPending()): its callback sends ServerboundResourcePackPacket, whose
+//    timing stays vanilla's;
+//  - extractRenderState(): the 0.5 s fade-in animation is skipped (opaque at once, as vanilla is after 0.5 s), and the
+//    in-world hold draws the opaque first stage of vanilla's fade-out (fadeOutAnim pinned to 0).
